## Original Content
DÉCRYPTAGE - Alors que les pensions représentent un quart de la dépense publique, les candidats à la fonction suprême seront bien obligés de prendre position.

## Summary
The article highlights the unavoidable issue of pensions in the 2027 French presidential election, emphasizing that pensions represent a quarter of public spending. Candidates will be compelled to address this contentious topic, which is complicating their campaigns.

## Key Points
- Pensions account for 25% of public spending in France.
- Candidates for the 2027 presidential election must take a position on pension reforms.
- The pension issue is described as unavoidable and poisoning the election campaign.


